# Findings that the security gate (ci/security_gate.py) accepts for a while.
# One entry per line. The date and the reason are both required.
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD reason:<one line>
# An image entry exempts a repository from the "no packages detected" failure only:
#         image <registry/repository> exp:YYYY-MM-DD reason:<one line>
# The expiry is at most 90 days away. Renew an entry when it expires.
# An entry that has expired, or lacks a reason, fails `make check-trivyignore`
# and blocks the gate.

image registry.k8s.io/pause exp:2027-01-31 reason:static binary, no OS packages
image docker.io/library/busybox exp:2027-01-31 reason:no OS release and no package database, so Trivy has nothing to match (verified with Trivy 0.76.1); its CVEs are not scanned
